s and Pronouns "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Demonstratives are words that show the person or thing you are talking about."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The demonstratives are: <span class=\"strong\"> this, that, these</span> and <span class=\"strong\"> those</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Demonstratives tell us about number (singular or plural) and distance (near or far)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are <span class=\"italic\"> demonstrative adjectives</span> and <span class=\"italic\"> demonstrative pronouns</span>. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "A demonstrative adjective tells us about the noun. It comes before the noun.<br /> <span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\"> This</span> potato is good.  <span class=\"strong\">That</span> potato is bad. <br/>I like <span class=\"strong\"> those</span> sweet potatoes. <span class=\"strong\"> These</span> large onions are on sale for $2.00 a pound. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "A demonstrative pronoun replaces a noun. It is on its own. <br /> <span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\"> This</span> is good.  <span class=\"strong\">That</span> is bad. <br/>I like <span class=\"strong\"> these</span>. I bake <span class=\"strong\"> those</span> once a month. </span> "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Asking Questions at the Supermarket"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can ask questions at the supermarket when you want to find something. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":\"02\",\"columns\":\"02\",\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Questions</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Examples </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Can you tell me where ... ?   <br />Where can I find ... ?  <br />Do you have any ... (in stock)?  <br />I am looking for (a) ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Can you tell where the sweet potatoes are?<br />  Where can I find potatoes? <br /> Do you have any onions in stock? <br /> I am looking for the apples on sale for $1.00. <br /> </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ingredient  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a food item used to prepare a dish"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I am looking for ingredients."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le04ob11aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are the words to review. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dish   "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "food that is prepared in a certain way "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I want to make a meat dish."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le04ob11aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to cook "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to prepare food to eat "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I love to cook."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le04ob11aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "recipe"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a set of instructions you use to make a certain dish "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The recipe calls for beef."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le04ob11aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "aisle "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "organized shelves for food or items "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The meat is in that aisle."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le04ob11aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "helpful "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "providing help "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You're very helpful."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le04ob11aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "checkout "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the place in a supermarket where you pay for your groceries  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Where is the checkout line?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le04ob11aud07"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn2le04ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write a dialogue (6-8 lines) between you and a supermarket clerk."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ask where items are."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Practice reading your dialogue aloud with a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I talk to a supermarket clerk. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I ask where things are in a supermarket."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I say how far or near things are."}]}], "type": "sena"}